## CI investigation: aggregate is correctly reporting unfinished issue scope

I investigated all three fresh `Issue 195 Full Acceptance` failures for head `2529023e280c670ac4c5928f34905c3370d98ea2`, including the latest [run 35899310366](https://github.com/link-foundation/meta-language/actions/runs/35899310366) and its [commit-bound report artifact](https://github.com/link-foundation/meta-language/actions/runs/35899310366/artifacts/10768603234).

This is not a flaky runner, stale SHA, merge conflict, dependency failure, or gate-integrity bug:

- manifest/protected-scope validation passes: 192 requirements and 249 fixture identities;
- the complete JavaScript suite passes: 129/129;
- the complete Rust suite passes: 470 unit/integration tests and 4 doc tests;
- the evaluator then correctly fails at 11/189 pre-merge requirements across 481 cells, with 0 gate errors.

The generated report identifies 178 genuinely incomplete rows. Across their cells there are 470 missing required result records, 356 references to planned but unpinned fixture artifacts, and 237 absent implementation entry points. The failed areas are: 57 default-CST rows, 40 four-language semantic rows, 32 structured-transformation rows, 12 directed translators, 5 embedded-language rows, 5 grammar importers, 5 parity rows, 4 binding-safe transformations, 4 external conformance rows, 4 generative-testing rows, 4 native-validation rows, 3 shared-concept rows, and 3 pre-merge package-delivery rows.

Disabling the workflow, making it non-blocking, deleting manifest rows, or manufacturing result JSON would directly violate the latest acceptance requirements. The PR remains draft, and I removed the reintroduced `Fixes #195` directive so merging this intermediate work cannot close the issue.

There is no legitimate narrow CI patch that can turn this aggregate green. Maintainer help is needed either to supply/allocate the missing language implementations, corpora, native toolchain validation, and cross-language preservation work in this PR, or to explicitly approve a scope split while retaining the fail-closed completion gate. Until then, the red aggregate is the truthful status required by the acceptance comment.
